WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.310
James wrote in, James says, Hey David, do
you think more Republicans don't stand up

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.920
to Trump because they're spineless or because
they're unprincipled?

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:12.300
I actually think there's a third option here
that you're not mentioning, which is an important

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.190
one, which is a lot of them do agree with
Trump.

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:21.140
So the 60 million people or whatever that
voted for Trump who also vote for senators

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.069
and members of Congress.

00:00:23.069 --> 00:00:29.810
Those senators and members of Congress may
have different reasons why they are not standing

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.789
up to Trump with what exceptions.

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:34.739
Like Justin Amash I hope is, I know it's not
a mash.

00:00:34.739 --> 00:00:40.260
I think I pronounced it a mash and someone
said it's Amash, Justin Amash and you know

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:45.730
Rick Wilson, who I interviewed on the program
or Kellyanne Conway's husband right there.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:47.590
There's a bunch of different things going
on.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:52.410
Some Republicans intellect that office aren't
standing up to Trump because they are spineless.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:57.909
They just are kind of go with the flow and
they don't want to rock the boat and they

00:00:57.909 --> 00:01:01.980
don't want to possibly have negative electorial
repercussions for their reelection campaigns

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.929
if they stand up to Trump.

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:08.740
Some are unprincipled in the sense that it's
all a power game to them it's sport.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:11.320
As I said before, it's about wins and losses.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:15.780
It doesn't matter if Obamacare is the same
thing that was proposed by the Heritage Foundation

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:19.909
in the 90s which is a very sort of corporatist
center, right?

00:01:19.909 --> 00:01:24.219
Plan to give tens of millions of new customers
to for-profit insurance companies.

00:01:24.219 --> 00:01:25.600
Doesn't matter.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.829
It's something that Obama did.

00:01:27.829 --> 00:01:28.829
It's a loss.

00:01:28.829 --> 00:01:33.180
And the way to put a box to check off a box
on the wind column is to repeal it and get

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.180
rid of it.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.780
Even if you would kick tens of millions of
people off of healthcare.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:37.780
It's just sport.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:41.890
And a lot of these Republicans really are
unprincipled and we know that because they

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:47.330
espouse one set of principles and then often
live by a completely different set of principles.

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:48.860
So that's group number two.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:51.130
There are also Republicans that just agree
with Trump.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:56.500
I mean at this point we have to sort of realize
that there are some Republicans who were just

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:01.229
kind of coalesced or emboldened to go public
with their beliefs and those beliefs always

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:03.149
matched many of Donald Trump's beliefs.

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:04.549
They just weren't saying it out loud.

00:02:04.549 --> 00:02:08.830
Now, a lot of people in the Trump era are
saying the quiet part outline out loud.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:14.070
There are also republicans that are, I mean
at this point there is such a thing as a Trumpist

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:18.480
republican that is a wing of the Republican
Party and some Republicans aren't standing

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.690
up to Trump because they simply agree with
the guy, so spineless and principled or or

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:24.720
agree with him.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:25.820
The answer is yes.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:29.500
All three of these, depending who you're talking
about for different people it is different

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:34.790
ones and this is why I've been now saying
for months Trump is going to go eventually.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.730
It could be in a year and a half.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:38.690
It could be in five and a half years.

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:45.450
But once he does, that doesn't mean that Trump
goes away unless we make it go away unless

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:50.780
we reject it completely and vote out and not
vote in all of the people that are subscribing

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:59.030
to this sort of coarsened, uh, outlandish
ignorance, uh, a glorification, that glorification

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:02.690
of ignorance that has taken place within Trump
and politics.

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:09.760
And this is why it's really important to understand
that Donald Trump was always, uh, some Donald

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:13.040
Trump is a symptom and not the disease, as
I've said before.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.480
And even when you cure the symptom of trumpet
by removing him, the disease that allowed

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:22.580
him to come to power in 2016 will still be
there unless we fully cure it.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:25.320
And that is why we need to be thinking beyond
just Trump and 2020.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:27.590
We need to be thinking about the House and
Senate.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:32.760
We need to be thinking about 20, 22 when Democrats
will have more possibilities to take over

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:37.030
control of the Senate, which I just don't
see any path to doing in 2020.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:39.020
We've got to be thinking bigger and beyond
Trump.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:43.470
And I think a lot of people in our audience,
at least from the emails I'm getting,

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.930
are thinking bigger in that way, which is
a good thing.

